68974 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "a5eebdd0-457e-5351-b479-fdec034c955a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069637 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069637 #edb/ref 1061 1800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069637 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d3ab3699-46bb-5348-b28d-d90ed53084d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069637 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069644 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069644 #edb/ref 1061 1801 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069644 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a1f73cdf-ffed-50a9-b236-c48f569059a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069644 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068743 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069648 #edb/ref 1061 1805 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069648 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fac6b988-f49b-56f2-aa72-c550c04fafb0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069648 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069723 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069723 #edb/ref 1061 26940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069723 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e2a84f61-3405-5b4c-a923-cf909df72a37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069723 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069724 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069724 #edb/ref 1061 27007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069724 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "08d4211a-dda1-5079-96e1-bb188234b652" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069724 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070036 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we are given the integral  $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{3x+2}{(x+1)^2} \\textrm{d}x.$ Note that we have the repeated factor $(x+1)$ in the denominator. \n\nThe correct form of the partial fraction expansion of the integrand is\n \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x+2}{(x+1)^2}=\\dfrac{A}{(x+1)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x+1)^2} \\,.\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A$ and $B,$ we first multiply both sides the above equation by $(x+1)^2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2 & =A(x+1)+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-1,$ we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-1)+2 & =A(-1+1)+B \\\\ B & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0$ and substituting the known value of $B,$ we can solve for $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)+2 & =A(0+1)+B \\\\ 2 & =A+B \\\\ 2 & =A-1 \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3x+2}{(x+1)^2}= \\dfrac{3}{(x+1)} -\\dfrac{1}{(x+1)^2}.\n$$\n\nNow this function can be integrated term by term. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3x+2}{(x+1)^{2}}\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{3}{(x+1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\int \\frac{1}{x+1}\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{(x+1)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{ln}|x+1|+\\frac{1}{x+1}+C\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant of integration." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070036 #edb/ref 1065 922 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070036 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "de271889-71f4-5fa2-8346-7ed8fa03e000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070036 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247455 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|-\\frac{1}{2x+1}+\\frac{1}{(2x+1)^{2}}+K" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247455 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186247455 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "043d1ce5-9e3e-5519-9a4c-03569c147664" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248193 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{1}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248193 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248193 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "554d505f-19eb-54e9-8916-dac052fc21dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248333 #edb/ref 1080 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2x+1|+\\frac{1}{2x+1}-\\frac{3}{4(2x+1)^{2}}+K" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186248333 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592